From: Sergey <onufriev.serg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: cfg80211: copy A-MSDU subframes into linear skbs

When the received A-MSDU lives in a page fragment, ieee80211_amsdu_to_8023s()
builds each subframe as a 32-byte head plus a fragment pointing into the
original buffer. On the EcoNet EN75xx the Ethernet QDMA has no scatter-gather
TX, so every such subframe is linearized again before it goes out: a second
allocation and a full copy per packet. Routing 5 GHz Wi-Fi to WAN on a
G-140W-C, memcpy was 15-17 % of the kernel CPU time.

Copy the subframe once, into a linear skb with the full headroom, instead.

--- a/net/wireless/util.c
+++ b/net/wireless/util.c
@@ -881,7 +881,12 @@ void ieee80211_amsdu_to_8023s(struct sk_
 		struct ethhdr eth;
 		uint8_t flags;
 	} hdr;
-	bool reuse_frag = skb->head_frag && !skb_has_frag_list(skb);
+	/*
+	 * Fragment-backed subframes are only cheaper when the Ethernet
+	 * driver can transmit them without linearizing; the EN75xx QDMA
+	 * cannot, so build every subframe as a single linear copy.
+	 */
+	bool reuse_frag = false;
 	bool reuse_skb = false;
 	bool last = false;
 	int copy_len = sizeof(hdr.eth);
